%%WIKI-SYNC-META%%
**Abstract.** Four personas, one per direct stakeholder in the Design Scenarios: Jan, the resident (HP-01); Myra, the care worker (HP-02); Sanne, the activity coordinator (HP-03); Kees, the walking partner (HP-04). All provisional: built from literature and group reasoning, not from interviews.

= Human Persona - Jan [HP-01] =

**Report Format:** §2.2 Personas and Profiles

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|HP-01
|Name|Jan, resident with dementia
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Literature and group reasoning only. Built on ST-01, PS-01 to PS-06.
|Elaborates|ST-01
|Role in Scenario|Walks the garden with Kees and the guide (DS-01). Sits at the window on rain days (DS-02). Rests and listens at dusk (DS-03).
|Task Demands|(((
1. Agree to go out
1. Keep the thread on the walk
1. Turn back from the gate
1. Calm down at dusk
1. Choose what to hear
)))
|Specific Capabilities and Needs|(((
Can: walk 20-30 minutes with a rollator, resting on benches; follow short, concrete sentences; answer yes or no; choose between two options.

Cannot: remember a list of options; recall this morning; find the way back alone.

Moderate dementia: recent memory poor; the years on the round vivid. Hearing aid, left ear.

Needs: a reason to go, a companion, time, plain adult speech.
)))
|Values and Motivations|(((
* HV-01 Autonomy - decides for themself; dislikes being "taken" for a walk
* HV-02 Dignity - thirty years of plain talk at front doors; wants to be spoken to plainly
* HV-03 Privacy - does not want staff to know every step
* HV-04 Safety - fell once; uneasy on gravel
* HV-05 Well-being - restless on days without going out
* HV-07 Social connectedness - misses the chats on the doorsteps
* HV-08 Identity - the post round, brass band, football: who Jan is
)))
|Social Network and Relationships|Daughter (ST-03) visits on Sundays and wrote the life story with Sanne. Kees (ST-04) lives two doors down. Myra (ST-02) is Jan's care worker most afternoons.
|History and Experiences|Thirty years as a postal worker, the last twenty on the same round, on foot and by bike. Walked the dog, Bram, twice a day until moving in two years ago. Refused a GPS watch: "I'm not a parcel."
|Constraints and Privacy Considerations|Will not be tracked. Will not wear anything on the head. Will not be quizzed: "I'm not at school."

= Human Persona - Myra [HP-02] =

**Report Format:** §2.2 Personas and Profiles

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|HP-02
|Name|Myra, care worker
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Literature and group reasoning only. Built on ST-02, SA-02, SA-06, PS-01, PS-05.
|Elaborates|ST-02
|Role in Scenario|Starts the walk, clips on the guide, returns to the ward (DS-01). Receives the gate alert and judges it from the window (DS-01). Starts lying practice at handover (DS-03).
|Task Demands|(((
1. Get residents out without walking every walk
1. Know quickly when someone needs help
1. Calm residents at handover
1. Read the record in seconds
)))
|Specific Capabilities and Needs|(((
Can: reassure, help physically, redirect; knows the residents well.

Needs: few, meaningful alerts; a phone message readable at a glance; devices that take seconds to set up.
)))
|Values and Motivations|(((
* HV-04 Safety - every resident back, unharmed
* HV-05 Well-being - residents out daily, calm in the evening
* HV-06 Attentive care - time for the resident who needs it now
* HV-01 Autonomy - lets residents choose, within time and safety limits
* HV-03 Privacy - for residents; and no timing of their own work
)))
|Social Network and Relationships|Six to eight residents per shift. Works with Sanne (ST-08). Employed by ST-05. Talks with families at visits.
|History and Experiences|Has run after residents at the gate. Has handed out the as-needed tablet at dusk when nobody could stay.
|Constraints and Privacy Considerations|Will not accept frequent low-value alerts. Will not accept a device that times their work.

= Human Persona - Sanne [HP-03] =

**Report Format:** §2.2 Personas and Profiles

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|HP-03
|Name|Sanne, activity coordinator
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Group reasoning only. Built on ST-08, SA-05, SA-07, PS-04, PS-06.
|Elaborates|ST-08
|Role in Scenario|Pairs Jan and Kees (DS-01). Sets up the rain-day session with Pepper (DS-02). Writes the life-story profiles with families.
|Task Demands|(((
1. Write and update profiles: welcome topics, avoided topics, favourites
1. Pair residents who will get on
1. Run sessions for more residents than they can sit beside
1. Keep content fresh
)))
|Specific Capabilities and Needs|(((
Can: talk with families; read a group; run the activity programme.

Not technical. Needs: a profile form that takes at most 20 minutes; sessions that start with one tap.
)))
|Values and Motivations|(((
* HV-05 Well-being - pleasant, meaningful days
* HV-08 Identity - activities that fit the person
* HV-07 Social connectedness - pairs and groups
* HV-06 Attentive care - time per resident
* HV-03 Privacy - the life stories in their care
)))
|Social Network and Relationships|Families (ST-03), volunteers (ST-07), care workers (ST-02), psychologist (ST-06).
|History and Experiences|Ran snoezel sessions with recorded relaxation, and watched residents get lost in them (PS-04).
|Constraints and Privacy Considerations|Will not keep a profile that families cannot see. Will not let Pepper replace activities with people.

= Human Persona - Kees [HP-04] =

**Report Format:** §2.2 Personas and Profiles

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|HP-04
|Name|Kees, walking partner
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Group reasoning only. Built on ST-04, SA-04, PS-02.
|Elaborates|ST-04
|Role in Scenario|Walks with Jan; talks about the post; presses pause when the talk is good (DS-01).
|Task Demands|(((
1. Join the walk
1. Talk
1. End the walk when they like
)))
|Specific Capabilities and Needs|(((
Can: walk without aid; talk easily; use one big button.

Mild dementia: forgets names; remembers faces.
)))
|Values and Motivations|(((
* HV-07 Social connectedness - company, a mate to talk to
* HV-01 Autonomy - free to say no, free to turn back
* HV-05 Well-being - own walk, own health
* HV-08 Identity - forty years sorting the post at the depot
* HV-02 Dignity - walks as Jan's partner; minding Jan is staff's job
)))
|Social Network and Relationships|Lives two doors from Jan. Own family; own care plan.
|History and Experiences|Sorted the post at the depot in the same town. Never met Jan there, as far as either remembers.
|Constraints and Privacy Considerations|Will not be responsible for Jan. If Jan wanders off, that is staff's job.
